Acoustic Connect for Cordova

New Features

- Opt-in remote kill switch control via `KillSwitchEnabled`/`KillSwitchUrl` in
  `ConnectConfig.json` — both native SDKs ship with the kill switch on by
  default, but this plugin forces it off unless the app explicitly opts in
- Opt-in location-logging control via `LocationLoggingEnabled` in
  `ConnectConfig.json` — tri-state: omit or set `null` to leave the native
  SDK's own default untouched, or explicitly opt in/out of location data
  collection
- `AndroidVersion`/`iOSVersion` config fields to pin a specific native Connect
  SDK version instead of the plugin's bundled default
- Analytics API in the JavaScript bridge: `logCustomEvent`, `logSignal`,
  `setCurrentScreenName`, `logScreenViewContextLoad`/`logScreenViewContextUnload`,
  `logClickEvent`, `logTextChangeEvent`, `logExceptionEvent`, `flushQueues`,
  `isSdkEnabled` and `getSdkVersion`, with TypeScript types. Text passed to
  `logTextChangeEvent` is masked by default before it leaves JavaScript
- `setConfigItem` / `getConfigItem` in the JavaScript bridge to set and read native
  SDK configuration items at runtime, with TypeScript types
- `ScreenCaptureEnabled` in `ConnectConfig.json` — set `false` to turn the SDK's
  layout and screenshot capture off on both platforms (screen views keep
  flowing). Omit it to keep the SDK default
- `layoutConfig`, `layoutConfigIos` and `layoutConfigAndroid` in
  `ConnectConfig.json` to deliver the SDK's screen-capture rules (`AutoLayout`,
  `AppendMapIds`), merged per platform
- Demo app: the Behaviour tab now exercises the analytics API

Fixes

- iOS rich push (NSE/NCE) extensions' `CFBundleVersion`/`CFBundleShortVersionString`
  now automatically track the host app's own version, fixing an App Store
  submission blocker (Apple rejects a mismatch between an app extension's
  version and its containing app's)
- Fixed a build failure when switching `useRelease` (Debug ↔ Release) via
  `cordova plugin rm`/`add` — a stale xcframeworks build-phase reference left
  over from the previous SDK variant is now cleaned up automatically, so a
  full `cordova platform rm`/`add ios` rebuild is no longer required
- Fixed duplicate push token-registration logs and a duplicate Cordova bridge
  callback warning on Android, caused by a race between the bundled auto-init
  path and an explicit `enable()` call both running push setup
- iOS `enable()` no longer blocks Cordova's own thread watchdog — native SDK
  initialization is now deferred by one run-loop turn instead of running
  synchronously on the calling thread


Known Issues

- Rich push cannot be end-to-end tested on the iOS Simulator — simulators don't display large icon.
- Clicks and typing inside the page are not captured automatically — call
  `logClickEvent`/`logTextChangeEvent` yourself. They are sent as custom events
- Native layout masking rules do not mask text inside the WebView; use
  `ScreenCaptureEnabled: false` to keep page content out of captures
- `layoutConfigAndroid` replaces the Android SDK's whole layout config; the
  effect of layout rules on Android has not been verified
- On Android the SDK drops a screen view whose screen name is still queued, so
  `logScreenViewContextUnload` for the screen just loaded rejects with
  `ACOUSTIC_INTERNAL_ERROR`; unload the previous screen instead
- `logCustomEvent` values are nested under `data.value` on iOS but flat on
  Android, and a `logSignal` payload under `signal.data.value` on iOS but at the
  root of `signal` on Android; `logSignal` drops a top-level number on Android
  SDKs before 11.0.24-beta (the default is 11.1.10-beta, which sends it)
- On iOS `logExceptionEvent` reports `stackTrace: (null)` and carries the stack
  text in `data.stacktrace`

Our environment for this release:

- Xcode 26.2
- MacOS 26.0.1
- iOS 15.1 to 26.x
- Android minSdk 26, SDK 36
